GCS-Pose

This package is derived from a PoseMamba/ReliPose research codebase and keeps
the original PoseMamba class for baseline comparison.  The selective-scan CUDA
sources are derived from the Mamba selective-scan implementation associated
with Albert Gu and Tri Dao; source-file copyright notices are retained where
present.  The project-level license is provided in LICENSE.

The package contains research modifications for fixed skeleton graph mixing,
factorized bidirectional state propagation, graph-conditioned selective-state
parameters, and a torch.compile-compatible wrapper around the existing CUDA
kernel.  It does not include datasets, pretrained weights, experiment outputs,
or third-party assets in the source tree. GCS-Pose model-only checkpoint exports
are distributed separately through this project's Releases.

Upstream projects:
PoseMamba: https://github.com/nankingjing/PoseMamba
Mamba: https://github.com/state-spaces/mamba

GCS-Pose is an independent research extension and is not an official PoseMamba
release. Inherited Mamba/selective-scan machinery, bidirectional scanning and
pose-lifting utilities are not claimed as original GCS-Pose contributions.
GCS-Pose modifications include factorized spatial/temporal recurrence, skeleton
graph mixing and context-conditioned selection (pose U/Z; graph-enhanced Delta/B/C).
This project name does not replace any upstream copyright or license notice.
